<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Confederation of the Rhine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Confederation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> was a union of German states formed in 1806 under the protection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. Its creation led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> to abdicate the imperial title later that year. It marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine.jpg" alt="Confederation of the Rhine" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Confederation_of_the_Rhine_(1812).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Defeat by Napoleon at the Battle of Austerlitz in December 1805 and the Peace of Pressburg cost Austria Tyrol, Vorarlberg and Venetia, and the formation of the <b>Confederation of the Rhine</b> in July 1806 made the old empire meaningless.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Both survived the Thirty Years War and the Napoleonic reorganisation of Germany, escaping mediatisation by joining the <b>Confederation of the Rhine</b> in 1806, and later became members of the German Confederation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-hohenzollern">County of Hohenzollern · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>By the Treaty of Posen in December 1806 Frederick Augustus made peace with Napoleon, joined the <b>Confederation of the Rhine</b> and took the title of king, ending the electorate a few months after the dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire.</blockquote><a href="/empire/electorate-of-saxony">Electorate of Saxony · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The German Confederation (Deutscher Bund) was created at the Congress of Vienna to fill the space left by the Holy Roman Empire, dissolved in 1806, and by Napoleon’s <b>Confederation of the Rhine</b>, which had collapsed after the Battle of Leipzig in 1813.</blockquote><a href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1806 he joined Napoleon's <b>Confederation of the Rhine</b> and took the title Grand Duke Louis I, gaining sovereignty and the lands of neighbouring counts and princes who were mediatised, among them Erbach, parts of Isenburg and Solms, the Burgraviate of Friedberg and Hesse-Homburg.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Grand Duchy of Hesse · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After the defeat at Austerlitz and the formation of the <b>Confederation of the Rhine</b>, he dissolved the Holy Roman Empire on 6 August 1806.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
